/* Bottom navigation — restyled to the V2 dark bar.
 * Spec: DESIGN_IMPLEMENTATION.md §4 "Bar spec"; token mapping: Appendix A.1.
 * Figma: `Pinned Bottom Navigation` 390x98 on every V2 frame (node 29:2154 et al).
 *
 * NOTE: no hex literals anywhere in this file, comments included —
 * TokenDisciplineTests.ComponentUss_HasNoHardcodedColors scans the raw text.
 *
 * GEOMETRY (transcribed literally — 1 USS px = 1 dp = 1 Figma pt, §1.2)
 *   container   inverse-surface fill, 1px primary (navy) top border
 *   tab row     390x64, horizontal, space-between, padding 0 24
 *   tab         64 wide, vertical, gap 4, centered
 *   active      56x32 pill, padding 4/16, radius 16, secondary (amber) fill,
 *               24dp icon tinted on-secondary (navy), label 600 11px white
 *   inactive    no pill, icon + label white at 50%, label 600 11px
 *
 * The 34dp OS home-indicator strip under the row is SAFE-AREA PADDING APPLIED BY THE
 * HOST, not a drawn element (§1, Appendix B). That is why the bar declares
 * `min-height` (a floor) rather than `height`, and why the 64dp row height lives on
 * the ITEM: a host `padding-bottom: 34px` then adds below a row that stays 64 tall,
 * giving the 98dp total, instead of squeezing the row inside a fixed box.
 *
 * WHY THE BASE RULES ARE THE *INACTIVE* LOOK
 *  USS has no `:not()`, so "inactive" cannot be selected directly. The base rules
 *  therefore describe the inactive destination and `--active` overrides it.
 *
 * INACTIVE LABEL WEIGHT IS 600 — AND THE FIGMA FILE DOES NOT AGREE WITH ITSELF
 *  This used to be documented as settled ("V2's inactive labels are 500"). It is not.
 *  4 of the 12 V2 frames draw the bar as 500 inactive / 600 active; the other 8 —
 *  including every higher, i.e. newer, node id — draw BOTH states at 600 and let the
 *  50%-strength ink carry the state on its own. Resolved in favour of **600**: the newer
 *  frames win, it matches the shared `.md-typescale-label-small` class, and a single
 *  face for both states means selecting a tab cannot re-measure the string. So the
 *  only thing `--active` now changes about the label is its ink color. `Inter-Medium`
 *  (500) is still in Fonts/ if the designer ever confirms the other reading; that is
 *  a one-line change to the rule below.
 *  Sizes/tracking match label-small (11px / ls 0) either way.
 *
 * "WHITE AT 50%" IS A PRE-BLENDED TOKEN, NOT AN opacity — AND THAT IS THE FIX
 *  Appendix A.1 maps the inactive tab's "white at 50%" to inverse-on-surface at 50%,
 *  and this used to author it as `color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface)` plus
 *  `opacity: 0.5`. That is correct arithmetic in Figma and wrong in Unity: the project
 *  renders in LINEAR color space, so the blend happens after an sRGB->linear convert
 *  and lands too light — measured (183,184,185) against the design's (127,130,136).
 *  The inactive tabs read almost as bright as the active one, which is the entire
 *  state distinction gone. The bar is an OPAQUE inverse-surface, so the composite is
 *  knowable exactly and is authored as the token `inverse-on-surface-muted`
 *  (Tokens/_brand-*.uss, per theme because both the ink and the bar flip). Active
 *  therefore switches COLOR rather than opacity. Still no literal, still re-themeable.
 *
 * ONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION: THE PILL BOX IS UNCONDITIONAL
 *  V2's tabs are 41dp (inactive) and 49dp (active) tall, both centred in the 64dp row,
 *  so its inactive labels sit ~4dp HIGHER than the active one. Here the 56x32 box is
 *  always present and only its fill changes, which:
 *    - keeps every icon centre exactly where V2 puts it (23.5dp down the row, identical
 *      in both designs — the deviation is only that inactive labels join the active
 *      one's baseline instead of floating 4dp above it);
 *    - keeps the active/inactive switch a pure repaint, with no layout jump under the
 *      background-color transition;
 *    - keeps the state layer's rounded, clipped host alive for inactive presses;
 *    - avoids clipping the glyph: TextCore's line box for a 24px font is taller than
 *      24px, so a 24x24 `overflow: hidden` host would crop it.
 */

.md-nav-bar {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 64px;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 24px;
    padding-right: 24px;
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-surface);
    /* DELIBERATE 1dp OVERSHOOT: this hairline sits outside the 98dp fill (64dp row +
     * the host's 34dp safe-area padding), so the bar measures 99dp against V2's 98.
     * Leave it. The 98 is a fill height and every content position inside it measured
     * exact, so any change that recovers the dp has to move content off spec — and
     * UI Toolkit has no box-shadow, which makes this border the project's accepted
     * substitute for V2's shadowed bar edge. */
    border-top-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
}

/* One destination. Fixed 64dp width + space-between is what makes 3, 4 or 5
 * destinations all lay out without touching this file (5 x 64 = 320 <= 342dp of
 * content width at 390dp). `flex-shrink: 0` keeps that true at the 5-tab end. */
.md-nav-bar__item {
    width: 64px;
    height: 64px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}

/* Icon host — the active-indicator pill: 56x32, padding 4/16 around the 24dp icon.
 * Transparent when inactive (V2: "no pill"), amber when active; see the deviation
 * note in the header for why the BOX is unconditional and only the fill moves. */
.md-nav-bar__indicator {
    width: 56px;
    height: 32px;
    padding: 4px 16px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-large);
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition-property: background-color;
    transition-duration: var(--md-sys-motion-duration-short2);
}

.md-nav-bar__indicator .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface);
}

.md-nav-bar__icon {
    font-size: 24px;
    color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface-muted);
}

/* Label — label-small metrics (11px / ls 0) at the 600 face (see the weight note
 * in the header). `margin-top: 4px` is V2's `gap: 4`; USS has no `gap`.
 *
 * Deliberately NOT clipped: V2 lets a long label ("Avistamentos", ~71dp) overflow the
 * 64dp tab symmetrically rather than ellipsize it, and space-between leaves room.
 *
 * `width: 100%` + `middle-center` IS THAT SYMMETRY, and it is not decoration. A flex
 * child wider than its line is clamped to FLEX-START by Yoga rather than centred, so
 * an auto-width label that outgrows its tab silently stops obeying the item's
 * `align-items: center` — and "Avistamentos" is the only one of the four that does,
 * which is why tab 4 alone rendered ~3.75dp left of its own icon. Pinning the box to
 * the tab's 64dp and letting TextCore centre the string inside it puts the overhang
 * on both sides. The other three labels fit, so centring inside 64dp is a no-op
 * for them. */
.md-nav-bar__label {
    margin-top: 4px;
    padding: 0;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-SemiBold.asset");
    color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface-muted);
    white-space: nowrap;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* ---- Active destination ---- */

.md-nav-bar__item--active .md-nav-bar__indicator {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-secondary);
}
.md-nav-bar__item--active .md-nav-bar__icon {
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-secondary);
}
/* Same 600 face as the base rule (restated so the pair is readable at a glance, and
 * so flipping the inactive weight back to 500 stays a one-line change up there);
 * the ink COLOR is what actually moves between the two states — see the header note
 * on why this is a token swap and not an opacity. */
.md-nav-bar__item--active .md-nav-bar__label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-SemiBold.asset");
    color: var(--md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface);
}
/* Ripple on the amber pill must be the on-color, not white. */
.md-nav-bar__item--active .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-on-secondary);
}

/* ---- Interaction states ---- */

.md-nav-bar__item:hover .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-hover-opacity);
}
.md-nav-bar__item:focus .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-focus-opacity);
}
.md-nav-bar__item:active .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-pressed-opacity);
}
